  "notes": "A claim whose only verifying attestation has 5 confirmations is unanchored and holds nothing (§8.2.5 (1)). A proof over another digest anchors nothing. When the lowest attestation's header has another Merkle root, or the chain has no block at its height (at or below the reader's tip), the claim is unanchored at any tip, though the higher attestation verifies, and the higher header is never read: `unread_heights_with_wrong_low_root` lists a height whose read would fail, and the answer is still null. Until 2026-10-26 the 0.4.0 draft passed over such a lowest attestation to the next."
